Parse the SECTORS-PER-TRACK field with strtoull() instead of strtoll().

ONE INSERTED CHARACTER at diskimage.c:1698, inside `case 'g':` of the -d prefix parser.
The heads field five lines above keeps strtoll, which is what makes it a plausible
half-done edit rather than a rewrite.

This is the mutant diff_diskimage_geom.c documents as FAMILY C (:605) and records as a
MEASURED evasion: it "passed all 30 rows" of that file's previous version, because every
other geometry vector in the file is non-negative.  strtoull() applies a leading minus
in UNSIGNED arithmetic, so `-d g16;-18446744073709551615:` converts to spt = 1 and is
ACCEPTED, while strtoll() underflows to LLONG_MIN and the range check rejects it.  A
plain "-1" does NOT discriminate -- both parses land below 1 and both reject -- which is
why the row's vector is -ULLONG_MAX and why nothing cheaper can stand in for it.

It is the edit a maintainer might make in good faith: "heads and sectors per track are
counts, they cannot be negative, so use the unsigned parse."  The reasoning is wrong
only because of a C library surprise, which is precisely the kind of defect a
differential exists to catch.

Chosen because it is the tightest control available for this file: MEASURED, 34 rows /
0 failures pristine and 34 rows / 1 failure mutant, and the single red row is the one
this control is pinned to.  Witness line from the mutant arm:
  FAIL bound: -ULLONG_MAX must not fold to 1 in the SPT position ACCEPTED (want
  reject); C/H/S=1280/16/1 blocks=20480

Deliberately NOT the two other single-row candidates the file documents: `if (prefix_g)`
-> `if (prefix_g && !prefix_f)` (killed only by the fg2;9 row) and the floppy divisor
512 -> 511 (killed only by the "NOT a multiple of 81920" row).  Both would work; this
one was preferred because it is a one-character edit in the SUBJECT and because the row
it pins guards a parse defect that no boot gate can reach.

Deliberately NOT anything in diskimage_recalc_size()'s shared cylinder block: mutants
there are caught by six or more rows at once, and the file's own header already records
five of them as PROVABLY EQUIVALENT -- an equivalent mutant would report SELFMUTANT_FAIL
forever for a reason that is not a defect.
